WEBVTT

00:42:27.694 --> 00:42:31.086
or might the country,
and not just this country, other countries

00:42:31.110 --> 00:42:33.194
change in response
to some of this thinking?

00:42:33.218 --> 00:42:36.578
DB: Yeah, Robert Putnam
has a theory which I agree with,

00:42:36.602 --> 00:42:38.119
or at least I learned from him,

00:42:38.143 --> 00:42:41.403
which is, he looked at moments
of social change, big change;

00:42:41.427 --> 00:42:44.744
and 1890 to 1910 was such a moment.

00:42:44.768 --> 00:42:47.372
It was a period when we had
a big wave of immigration,

00:42:47.396 --> 00:42:50.216
a big economic transition,
a lot of political corruption ...

00:42:50.240 --> 00:42:52.400
And he said, "How did change happen?"

00:42:52.424 --> 00:42:54.633
He said, "First, it happened culturally.

00:42:54.657 --> 00:42:57.524
The social gospel movement
replaced social Darwinism,

00:42:57.548 --> 00:43:01.169
so a very individualistic ethos
was replaced by a communitarian ethos.